+
+## Importing from CSV
+
+Pick a file with the control on the page, or drop it onto that panel. A typical
+input is `example.csv`.
+
+- **Headers.** The first row must identify 姓名 and 邮箱; 公司 is optional. English
+  headers (`name`, `email`/`e-mail`, `company`/`organization`) and a few common
+  variants are accepted. Unrecognized extra columns are ignored and reported.
+  If 姓名 or 邮箱 is missing, nothing is imported and the error names the expected
+  headers.
+- **Import is additive.** Existing contacts are never overwritten or deleted.
+  An imported row that exactly matches an existing contact (same name, email and
+  company; email compared case-insensitively) is skipped as a duplicate.
+- **Bad rows are skipped, not guessed.** A row missing a name or email, or with a
+  malformed email, is reported with its line number while the remaining rows still
+  import. A row with more columns than the header — the signature of a comma that
+  was not quoted — is rejected rather than mapped by position, because the shift
+  would put values in the wrong columns.
+- **Quoting** follows RFC 4180: fields containing commas or line breaks must be
+  wrapped in double quotes, and a literal quote is written twice (`""`).
+- **Encoding.** UTF-8 is assumed first. If the file is not valid UTF-8 it is read
+  as GB18030/GBK, which is what Excel writes on a Chinese Windows system, and the
+  page says so. GB18030 is not available in every browser (notably some Safari
+  versions), in which case a UTF-8 best-effort decode is used and disclosed.
+- **Undo.** After an import that added contacts, the summary offers an undo that
+  restores the list as it was before that import.
+- **Session only.** Imported contacts are not persisted. Reloading the page
+  returns the list to the three built-in contacts.
